title: Debug log prints request bodies including passwords
updated: 2026-10-13T19:50:28Z
---

`_build_request` logs every request body verbatim at debug level (`lib/WWW/Hetzner/Role/HTTP.pm:230-233`, `$log->debugf("Body: %s", ...)`). Bodies that carry secrets go through it unchanged: Storage Box create / reset_password and subaccount create / reset password (`password`), Cloud server create (`user_data`, often carrying credentials), certificate upload (`private_key`).

WWW::MikroTik solved the same problem with a structural mask for the debug line only (`p5-www-mikrotik/lib/WWW/MikroTik.pm:610-617`).

Done when: the debug line masks top-level keys such as `password`, `private_key`, `user_data` (the request itself unchanged), documented in the Role::HTTP POD and covered in `t/logging.t`.

